# Line endings are normalised to LF in the repository and checked out as LF
# everywhere, Windows included.
#
# Without this, the Windows runner checks out CRLF, and a file the build
# swallows whole stops matching what the code expects of it. That is how
# `skill_carries_the_running_version` started failing: `hoard agents` embeds
# `SKILL.md` with `include_str!` at compile time and asserts the frontmatter
# opens with `---\n`, which a CRLF checkout turns into `---\r\n`. The test was
# the messenger; the shipped binary would have carried the CRLF too. Every
# other `include_str!` in the tree is exposed the same way, the panel locales
# among them.
#
# Nothing in the tree wants CRLF. The PowerShell installer and the NSIS hook
# are both LF already and both interpreters read LF fine.
* text=auto eol=lf
